    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are staring down a slate where our focus shifts toward speed and matchup optimization against vulnerable pitching. **Nasim Nunez** earns the highest projection of the day at 64.14, benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against Ryan Feltner (5.10 xERA). With stolen bases remaining our scarcest commodity, **Nasim Nunez** is an auto-start; the +19% boost from Feltner\u2019s inability to suppress baserunners positions him as our primary spark plug. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (59.34) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.63) are strong secondary plays against Kumar Rocker. While Rocker\u2019s 4.36 xERA isn\u2019t bottom-tier, the offensive environments and their high-leverage spots in the order (#1 and #3, respectively) provide the volume necessary to stabilize our R/RBI output.\n\nOur most critical lineup decision today involves **Tommy White** (55.05) and **Jackson Merrill** (51.55), who occupy the middle-order spots. **Tommy White** is the superior play here due to a +10% park factor advantage, which edges out the risk associated with facing Zebby Matthews. Conversely, **Jackson Merrill** faces a tougher test against Braxton Ashcraft (3.28 xERA), but his dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier. **Liam Hicks** remains our most volatile play at 49.04; while his #4 spot provides RBI potential, the -11% penalty from the platoon disadvantage against Framber Valdez makes him a marginal start that we will monitor closely once the official lineups lock.\n\nIt is worth noting that our elite core of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are all currently unavailable due to team off-days, leaving the heavy lifting to the depth pieces like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, all of whom are currently relegated to the bench. Given the volatility of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Liam Hicks** and **Nasim Nunez**, we are keeping **Jacob Wilson** and **Heliot Ramos** ready as high-floor pivots should any of our starters be rested for late-August fatigue. We are operating with a cautious approach today, prioritizing the speed categories through **Nasim Nunez** while tempering expectations for power-heavy bats like **Tommy White** until we see the wind and weather reports finalize.",
